\item date: 09/01/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo, Elly van Munster\\
Changed into a real agreement-rule (instead of making four paths, of which
later on three are filtered out in the substitution-rules).
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] 
( Franciska: To account for all morphological variants of adjs. )\\
The rule is ordered in subgrammar ADJPPROPtoADJPFORMULA
in parallel to TC:TSVagr. The results of this rule class are relevant for
adjs that are substituted for CNVAR in NPs, for
CLOSEDadjpprops, as well as for the translation
of ADJPs sec.\\
(Franciska: Adjs with .thetaadj = adjp000 are always singular and masculine.
This fact is accounted for in RSTARTADJPPROP000 ) ?????\\
